1
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:43,544
Get down.

2
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:48,924
I said get down.

3
00:00:49,008 --> 00:00:49,967
What?

4
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:52,344
Get down!

5
00:01:02,521 --> 00:01:04,023
What the sh…

6
00:01:06,442 --> 00:01:07,485
That scared me!

7
00:01:19,121 --> 00:01:20,164
It's all right now.

8
00:01:21,373 --> 00:01:22,291
It's over.

9
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:33,427
Get up slowly.

10
00:01:33,511 --> 00:01:34,595
Your muscles must be in shock.

11
00:01:44,146 --> 00:01:45,439
Thank you.

12
00:01:45,523 --> 00:01:48,692
What on earth just happened?

13
00:01:48,776 --> 00:01:50,903
The fire suppression sprinkler exploded.

14
00:01:51,737 --> 00:01:53,197
It must've been defective.

15
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:56,826
Not even the cheapest ones
would explode like that.

16
00:01:57,827 --> 00:01:58,911
Which brand is it?

17
00:01:58,994 --> 00:02:00,788
Was it installed a long time ago?

18
00:02:01,914 --> 00:02:03,749
Did you notice anything unusual about it?

19
00:02:06,877 --> 00:02:09,213
I'm not really sure.

20
00:02:10,339 --> 00:02:11,632
When did we install it again?

21
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:13,592
Was it about six months ago?

22
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:16,387
We were short on cash

23
00:02:17,012 --> 00:02:19,139
-so we got a bootleg.
-What?

24
00:02:19,723 --> 00:02:21,684
"Bootleg"?

25
00:02:23,769 --> 00:02:25,521
Hey, Song-yi.

26
00:02:27,106 --> 00:02:28,649
Someone's here.

27
00:02:36,615 --> 00:02:40,202
I don't know how to express
my gratitude for your visit.

28
00:02:41,078 --> 00:02:43,581
But I must also say I'm truly sorry.

29
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:46,876
There's been an unexpected issue
in the kitchen,

30
00:02:46,959 --> 00:02:49,378
and I'm afraid
we can't serve dinner tonight.

31
00:02:51,297 --> 00:02:53,924
I'm terribly sorry.

32
00:02:59,305 --> 00:03:00,931
I heard something explode.

33
00:03:01,015 --> 00:03:03,434
Is everything okay?
Should we call emergency services?

34
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:05,269
Oh, no.

35
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:06,854
Everything is fine now.

36
00:03:06,937 --> 00:03:08,939
The staff is cleaning up the mess.

37
00:03:09,648 --> 00:03:10,566
That's a relief.

38
00:03:12,359 --> 00:03:14,570
I don't know exactly what happened,

39
00:03:14,653 --> 00:03:16,989
but is there no way you can cook?

40
00:03:17,573 --> 00:03:20,367
We have a guest who made a long trip

41
00:03:20,451 --> 00:03:22,411
to taste Famiglia's food again
after a long time.

42
00:03:25,664 --> 00:03:26,540
Please.

43
00:03:27,249 --> 00:03:28,417
Do me a favor.

44
00:03:29,627 --> 00:03:31,045
It's been ten years.

45
00:03:38,177 --> 00:03:39,053
I'm…

46
00:03:40,930 --> 00:03:42,806
I'm so sorry.

47
00:03:46,352 --> 00:03:49,146
If you're an old regular
who loved our food…

48
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:55,027
Then I really don't think
we can serve you tonight.

49
00:03:56,111 --> 00:03:57,363
Serving poor quality

50
00:03:57,947 --> 00:04:02,117
in a situation like this
would dishonor my father.

51
00:04:19,426 --> 00:04:21,136
But I understand.

52
00:04:25,057 --> 00:04:27,559
It's a shame, but I see what you mean.

53
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:31,772
I guess we should head back then.

54
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,525
Henri Bernier?

55
00:04:35,859 --> 00:04:37,152
What is he doing here?

56
00:04:38,862 --> 00:04:39,738
Who?

57
00:04:40,364 --> 00:04:41,281
Henri who?

58
00:04:46,912 --> 00:04:47,997
Are you all right?

59
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:49,832
Did we land on some battlefield?

60
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:52,209
Hey, are you all right?

61
00:04:53,127 --> 00:04:55,713
Get up slowly.

62
00:04:57,381 --> 00:04:58,799
Oh my god. Did you hit your head?

63
00:04:58,882 --> 00:05:00,509
-Yes.
-Let me see.

64
00:05:02,553 --> 00:05:03,554
Is it bleeding?

65
00:05:07,891 --> 00:05:08,726
Are you okay?

66
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:11,979
Yes, I'm fine.

67
00:05:13,105 --> 00:05:14,189
I'm really fine.

68
00:05:18,152 --> 00:05:19,069
Thank you.

69
00:05:29,788 --> 00:05:32,207
I didn't expect
something like that to happen.

70
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:35,127
Why don't we just go to Exception instead?

71
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:36,670
We can have a glass of wine there.

72
00:05:37,463 --> 00:05:38,297
No, thank you.

73
00:05:39,548 --> 00:05:41,508
Hearing about Chef Choi's passing

74
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:43,677
has weighed on me.

75
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:47,639
I just arrived today,
so I'm tired as well.

76
00:05:49,308 --> 00:05:50,809
Let's visit Exception some other time.

77
00:05:58,150 --> 00:06:00,694
Well, if that's what you wish. No problem.

78
00:06:01,987 --> 00:06:03,781
I can catch a taxi across the street.

79
00:06:05,824 --> 00:06:08,494
Thank you for coming
to pick me up today, Ms. Baek.

80
00:06:08,577 --> 00:06:11,246
And you too, Ms. Seon.

81
00:06:12,915 --> 00:06:16,335
I'll have your luggage sent to your hotel.

82
00:06:17,336 --> 00:06:18,212
Thank you.

83
00:06:28,138 --> 00:06:31,183
Why did everything fall apart
at the last minute?

84
00:06:31,266 --> 00:06:34,103
He's our most important guest
and this is just day one!

85
00:06:34,686 --> 00:06:35,771
I swear,

86
00:06:35,854 --> 00:06:39,149
nothing ever goes right
whenever Famiglia is involved.

87
00:06:42,402 --> 00:06:43,529
You know,

88
00:06:44,071 --> 00:06:45,906
there are two types of people
in the world.

89
00:06:47,199 --> 00:06:49,493
People who make the impossible possible,

90
00:06:50,786 --> 00:06:52,913
and people who make
the possible impossible.

91
00:06:56,375 --> 00:06:58,377
Did you see that girl's facial features?

92
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:01,296
She looks just like her father.
I bet she's just as stubborn.

93
00:07:02,631 --> 00:07:05,342
This won't be easy for me.

94
00:07:06,135 --> 00:07:08,804
My brain… I have a headache.

95
00:07:08,887 --> 00:07:11,348
Where are my antacids?
Why isn't Hyeong-koo back yet?

96
00:07:11,974 --> 00:07:14,309
What did you say? Henri Bernier?

97
00:07:14,393 --> 00:07:16,145
You mean the man who was just here

98
00:07:16,228 --> 00:07:18,647
was the world-famous chef Henri Bernier?

99
00:07:27,281 --> 00:07:28,991
Did he have to come today of all days?

100
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:34,872
He said he missed Dad's food so much

101
00:07:35,581 --> 00:07:37,541
that he had come back after ten years.

102
00:07:38,417 --> 00:07:41,879
And I sent away
a special customer like him

103
00:07:42,921 --> 00:07:44,214
with the restaurant in this state.

104
00:07:45,299 --> 00:07:46,633
Song-yi.

105
00:07:46,717 --> 00:07:48,468
Go home and get some rest.

106
00:07:48,552 --> 00:07:50,220
The kitchen is mostly cleaned up now.

107
00:07:50,721 --> 00:07:52,556
I'll take a look at everything
thoroughly tomorrow.

108
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:55,559
I'm sorry.

109
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:57,644
It's all my fault.

110
00:09:13,303 --> 00:09:14,680
You're still here?

111
00:09:16,223 --> 00:09:18,558
SPICY CHICKEN WITH DRIED PERSIMMON

112
00:09:18,642 --> 00:09:21,186
I'll clean up the rest tomorrow.
You don't have to worry.

113
00:09:23,689 --> 00:09:26,024
CHICKEN SO GOOD IT STOPS A CRYING CHILD

114
00:09:26,608 --> 00:09:28,193
Sir, can you please…

115
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:31,154
Why do we offer a crying child
a dried persimmon?

116
00:09:32,739 --> 00:09:36,159
Why does a child who won't stop crying
even when they hear a tiger will eat them

117
00:09:36,827 --> 00:09:38,870
only stop crying
when they're offered a dried persimmon?

118
00:09:42,374 --> 00:09:43,292
It's because…

119
00:09:47,212 --> 00:09:49,381
the best remedy for sadness…

120
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:55,429
is nothing other than…

121
00:10:04,688 --> 00:10:06,815
delicious food.

122
00:10:12,779 --> 00:10:15,157
How long have you been cooking?
What's your position?

123
00:10:16,325 --> 00:10:17,534
I've been cooking for a year,

124
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,619
and I'm still a commis.

125
00:10:19,703 --> 00:10:21,538
COMMIS:
A JUNIOR-LEVEL KITCHEN STAFF MEMBER

126
00:10:22,372 --> 00:10:26,001
By the way, what is it that you do?

127
00:10:45,562 --> 00:10:46,813
We're only serving one guest,

128
00:10:46,897 --> 00:10:49,900
but they're a super VIP,
more important than anyone.

129
00:10:51,568 --> 00:10:53,528
Today's signature course

130
00:10:53,612 --> 00:10:55,864
will have five dishes,
from an antipasto to a dessert.

131
00:10:57,741 --> 00:10:59,618
I'd like you to serve dinner tonight.

132
00:10:59,701 --> 00:11:01,912
Let's get it done in two hours, okay?

133
00:11:01,995 --> 00:11:02,996
Okay.

134
00:11:04,373 --> 00:11:05,832
First, the antipasto.

135
00:11:05,916 --> 00:11:06,750
Scallops.

136
00:11:07,501 --> 00:11:08,752
When searing scallops,

137
00:11:08,835 --> 00:11:12,047
wait until the pan is smoking hot
before you start cooking.

138
00:11:12,130 --> 00:11:14,341
-Screaming hot, okay?
-Okay.

139
00:11:15,092 --> 00:11:16,635
Sear each side for five seconds.

140
00:11:16,718 --> 00:11:19,346
SEARING:
BROWNING THE OUTSIDE OVER HIGH HEAT

141
00:11:19,429 --> 00:11:22,349
That gives you a crispy outside
and a moist, medium center.

142
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:30,315
The scallops are only about 80% fresh, so…

143
00:11:32,609 --> 00:11:34,820
We'll go with something
other than the classic vongole.

144
00:11:35,404 --> 00:11:37,781
The clams weren't purged right,
and they smelled bad too.

145
00:11:58,885 --> 00:12:01,596
Finely slice the ingredients,
add them to a pot of oil,

146
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:03,181
and warm them slowly over low heat.

147
00:12:03,723 --> 00:12:05,267
"Slowly over low heat."

148
00:12:07,936 --> 00:12:10,105
Then cook everything for ten minutes
over medium heat.

149
00:12:11,022 --> 00:12:11,982
And then?

150
00:12:13,358 --> 00:12:14,317
Blend it into a purée

151
00:12:14,818 --> 00:12:16,945
with a teaspoon each
of brown rice vinegar and soy milk.

152
00:12:40,010 --> 00:12:41,511
Antipasto, scallops.

153
00:12:42,554 --> 00:12:45,390
ANTIPASTO
SEARED SCALLOPS WITH CHORIZO SAUCE

154
00:13:13,084 --> 00:13:15,045
Wait, my phone.

155
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:03,843
The scallops

156
00:14:05,262 --> 00:14:06,179
are perfect.

157
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:11,059
They were seared to perfection,

158
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:13,687
but they weren't as fresh
as they should've been.

159
00:14:14,813 --> 00:14:18,233
So he chose a chorizo sauce
with a strong, meaty flavor to mask it.

160
00:14:19,317 --> 00:14:21,152
Primo piatti, ravioli.

161
00:14:21,736 --> 00:14:22,612
Ravioli!

162
00:14:24,447 --> 00:14:26,741
The shrimp in the ravioli seemed spoiled.

163
00:14:27,701 --> 00:14:29,035
When were they made?

164
00:14:30,161 --> 00:14:31,580
About three days ago?

165
00:14:36,835 --> 00:14:37,669
Five days ago.

166
00:14:42,048 --> 00:14:43,049
A week ago.

167
00:14:47,137 --> 00:14:48,138
What about the pasta?

168
00:14:48,221 --> 00:14:51,975
We normally use fresh pasta, not dried,

169
00:14:52,058 --> 00:14:55,270
but our chef de partie quit earlier today.

170
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:07,032
FISHCAKE

171
00:15:08,491 --> 00:15:09,534
EGGPLANT

172
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:15,832
SUGAR

173
00:15:18,835 --> 00:15:21,129
We'll serve pasta as the primo
instead of ravioli.

174
00:15:21,212 --> 00:15:23,340
But we'll make the noodles with fishcakes.

175
00:15:24,799 --> 00:15:26,051
Fishcake noodles?

176
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:28,970
First, let's make the tomato sauce.

177
00:16:33,159 --> 00:16:35,787
EGGPLANT PASTA WITH FISHCAKE NOODLES

178
00:16:37,789 --> 00:16:40,166
Primo, tomato pasta. Go.

179
00:16:47,090 --> 00:16:48,550
I left my phone behind.

180
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:53,138
The primo piatti is a tomato…

181
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,516
It's a tomato sauce-based pasta.

182
00:16:58,685 --> 00:17:02,939
Didn't you say your kitchen
was in no state to cook in tonight?

183
00:17:03,565 --> 00:17:06,234
It wasn't, but…

184
00:17:20,999 --> 00:17:24,419
PROJECTED REVENUE STRUCTURE
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

185
00:17:27,464 --> 00:17:32,469
WHAT IS THE TABLE?
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026 SHOW CONCEPT

186
00:17:34,596 --> 00:17:36,890
THE WORLD'S BEST K-FOOD CHEF

187
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:41,561
"The world's best K-food chef…"

188
00:17:58,495 --> 00:17:59,454
What's this?

189
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,290
I think it's fishcake.

190
00:18:03,833 --> 00:18:04,709
Fishcake?

191
00:18:26,773 --> 00:18:28,566
The risotto rice was dry and crumbly.

192
00:18:30,235 --> 00:18:32,278
That's probably because the rice is old.

193
00:18:32,862 --> 00:18:34,989
Our supplier stopped importing
arborio rice for the risotto,

194
00:18:35,573 --> 00:18:37,659
so we had to use the cheap rice
meant for staff meals.

195
00:18:39,285 --> 00:18:41,830
Do you have any other grain,
like barley or mixed grains?

196
00:18:41,913 --> 00:18:43,665
We do have barley.

197
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:45,875
Oh, there's millet too.

198
00:18:59,722 --> 00:19:00,557
Okay.

199
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,002
The firm, springy texture
of barley and millet

200
00:19:29,878 --> 00:19:33,548
will definitely give it more chew
than a rice-based risotto.

201
00:19:35,008 --> 00:19:36,509
To maximize that texture…

202
00:19:44,017 --> 00:19:45,810
Forget the spinach. We need seafood.

203
00:19:45,894 --> 00:19:48,062
All we have are the scallops from earlier

204
00:19:48,146 --> 00:19:49,606
and the smelly clams.

205
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:52,609
I saw a market on the way here.

206
00:19:52,692 --> 00:19:54,652
-How far is it?
-To the market?

207
00:19:55,278 --> 00:19:56,571
A quick trip takes about 20 minutes.

208
00:19:57,572 --> 00:19:58,990
-Cuttlefish.
-What?

209
00:19:59,782 --> 00:20:00,950
Cuttlefish. In ten minutes.

210
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:04,078
Quick. Hurry. Let's go!

211
00:20:05,079 --> 00:20:05,955
Wait.

212
00:20:06,706 --> 00:20:09,459
And a bag of mixed nuts
with lots of macadamia nuts.

213
00:20:10,501 --> 00:20:11,377
And a can of peaches.

214
00:20:13,546 --> 00:20:15,256
Please. I'm counting on you.

215
00:20:18,384 --> 00:20:19,260
One more thing.

216
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:23,556
There's a shop that sells oil.

217
00:20:24,599 --> 00:20:26,517
Ask the lady
for a bottle of fresh pine nut oil.

218
00:20:28,811 --> 00:20:29,687
Pine nut oil…

219
00:20:50,667 --> 00:20:52,752
The texture alone isn't enough.

220
00:20:53,461 --> 00:20:54,671
It needs an aroma too.

221
00:20:54,754 --> 00:20:55,922
Something powerful.

222
00:20:57,173 --> 00:20:58,132
What can I use?

223
00:21:25,868 --> 00:21:26,703
WALNUTS

224
00:22:46,657 --> 00:22:48,826
Why is he grinding that by hand?

225
00:22:49,535 --> 00:22:52,872
Does food taste better when made by hand?

226
00:22:54,457 --> 00:22:55,458
Chef?

227
00:23:03,466 --> 00:23:04,300
Bingo.

228
00:23:29,742 --> 00:23:31,536
CUTTLEFISH RISOTTO

229
00:23:43,673 --> 00:23:44,715
What is this?

230
00:23:46,509 --> 00:23:47,885
The rice and cuttlefish both

231
00:23:48,803 --> 00:23:49,762
taste insane.

232
00:23:53,641 --> 00:23:56,185
I think it's made with barley
and something else.

233
00:23:58,729 --> 00:24:00,648
What is this unique aroma, Ms. Choi?

234
00:24:36,726 --> 00:24:37,727
Latex gloves.

235
00:25:18,351 --> 00:25:20,269
Burdock purée, squeeze bottle.

236
00:25:28,819 --> 00:25:30,738
Crown daisy pesto, small bottle.

237
00:26:22,123 --> 00:26:25,584
It looks like it's done.
Why isn't he telling me to serve it?

238
00:27:12,506 --> 00:27:17,928
BLACK GOAT STEAK IN PINE SMOKE

239
00:27:27,313 --> 00:27:28,356
This is just…

240
00:27:30,358 --> 00:27:31,317
I'm lost for words.

241
00:27:32,610 --> 00:27:35,571
Every dish was based on
classic Italian recipes,

242
00:27:35,654 --> 00:27:38,741
but each was given
a distinctly modern twist.

243
00:27:39,658 --> 00:27:42,286
Famiglia is without its head chef,
Choi Seung-hyo,

244
00:27:42,370 --> 00:27:43,788
and the food is still this amazing?

245
00:27:46,749 --> 00:27:48,584
Do excuse me. I need to use the restroom.

246
00:27:48,667 --> 00:27:49,585
Oh, sure.

247
00:28:25,413 --> 00:28:26,622
CHEF CHA

248
00:28:29,917 --> 00:28:30,751
Hey, Woo-jin.

249
00:28:32,795 --> 00:28:33,629
Well…

250
00:28:36,173 --> 00:28:37,383
It's a long story.

251
00:28:38,259 --> 00:28:39,927
Can I explain to you later?

252
00:29:00,281 --> 00:29:03,075
ORDER FOR TABLE 3

253
00:29:08,497 --> 00:29:10,708
Table three, two yuzu crème brûlées
and one fried green plum ice cream.

254
00:29:10,791 --> 00:29:12,626
-How long will it take?
-Two minutes, Chef.

255
00:29:12,710 --> 00:29:15,629
Table eight is still waiting for the main.
Where are the two quails?

256
00:29:15,713 --> 00:29:18,174
They're almost done.
We'll garnish and send them out.

257
00:29:18,257 --> 00:29:19,300
Work faster, everyone!

258
00:29:20,342 --> 00:29:21,510
We're behind schedule today.

259
00:29:21,594 --> 00:29:23,053
We've got two complaints already.

260
00:29:23,137 --> 00:29:24,388
-Yes, Chef!
-Yes, Chef!

261
00:29:37,151 --> 00:29:39,195
The dishes aren't entirely unfamiliar.

262
00:29:39,987 --> 00:29:43,032
But they all tasted completely new to me.

263
00:30:02,009 --> 00:30:03,052
Excuse me.

264
00:30:03,802 --> 00:30:06,889
Are you the chef
who prepared the food tonight?

265
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:09,642
Yes.

266
00:30:10,518 --> 00:30:13,270
I thought Famiglia
was missing a head chef.

267
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:15,981
Are you the new chef?

268
00:30:17,942 --> 00:30:19,109
No.

269
00:30:19,193 --> 00:30:21,529
I happened to cook just for tonight.

270
00:30:22,196 --> 00:30:23,113
Then may I ask

271
00:30:23,739 --> 00:30:27,076
which restaurant you work at?

272
00:30:30,704 --> 00:30:34,250
I'm just someone who happened to stop by.

273
00:30:37,461 --> 00:30:38,546
Goodbye.

274
00:30:39,505 --> 00:30:40,422
The food tonight…

275
00:30:45,469 --> 00:30:46,637
was quite impressive.

276
00:30:47,596 --> 00:30:50,140
I had to find out who had prepared it.

277
00:30:50,224 --> 00:30:51,642
I'm sorry if I was prying too much.

278
00:31:07,241 --> 00:31:08,200
Wait.

279
00:31:08,284 --> 00:31:09,702
They just served dessert.

280
00:31:09,785 --> 00:31:11,120
I'm sorry, Ms. Choi.

281
00:31:11,203 --> 00:31:12,705
I have to rush back.

282
00:31:13,914 --> 00:31:14,999
I see.

283
00:31:15,082 --> 00:31:17,334
Thank you so much for the meal.

284
00:31:17,418 --> 00:31:18,836
I really enjoyed it.

285
00:31:19,336 --> 00:31:21,422
I'll try the dessert next time.

286
00:31:24,341 --> 00:31:25,467
Just a moment.

287
00:31:31,599 --> 00:31:32,725
You didn't have to.

288
00:31:36,854 --> 00:31:38,939
The chef put a lot of work into it.

289
00:31:39,023 --> 00:31:40,608
It would be a shame to waste it.

290
00:31:40,691 --> 00:31:43,694
Be sure to put it in the fridge
if you want to eat it tomorrow.

291
00:31:45,571 --> 00:31:46,697
Thank you.

292
00:31:48,073 --> 00:31:49,992
-I'll see you around, Ms. Choi.
-Okay.

293
00:32:00,878 --> 00:32:02,880
Hey, I'm sorry to wake you.

294
00:32:02,963 --> 00:32:05,007
It must be dawn where you are.
Did I call too early?

295
00:32:06,300 --> 00:32:07,885
I know. That's how urgent this is.

296
00:32:08,594 --> 00:32:10,596
I just sent you a few photos.

297
00:32:11,764 --> 00:32:13,807
I think he's a chef.

298
00:32:13,891 --> 00:32:15,726
Find out quickly who he is.

299
00:32:17,895 --> 00:32:19,938
I don't know. I've never seen him before.

300
00:32:20,022 --> 00:32:21,899
I'll explain the details later.

301
00:32:21,982 --> 00:32:25,069
Ask a few people you can trust
and find out who he is.

302
00:32:26,612 --> 00:32:28,489
Okay. Call me right back.

303
00:32:44,922 --> 00:32:45,756
Goodness, my back.

304
00:33:17,162 --> 00:33:18,997
I hope the food was to your liking.

305
00:33:19,707 --> 00:33:22,626
I did my best,
but I didn't have the best ingredients.

306
00:33:22,710 --> 00:33:24,253
Not at all. It was good.

307
00:33:25,129 --> 00:33:28,257
I really enjoyed it.
I barely had time to think.

308
00:33:29,842 --> 00:33:30,759
I'm glad.

309
00:33:30,843 --> 00:33:32,636
Thank you so much.

310
00:33:33,387 --> 00:33:36,932
I could feel the heart and sincerity

311
00:33:38,100 --> 00:33:39,476
you put into your cooking.

312
00:33:40,185 --> 00:33:41,603
It felt like my dad's cooking.

313
00:33:46,483 --> 00:33:47,526
I apologize for earlier.

314
00:33:49,278 --> 00:33:51,071
I lashed out, not knowing the full story.

315
00:33:54,950 --> 00:33:57,286
I didn't know Chef Choi had passed away.

316
00:33:59,288 --> 00:34:00,122
I see.

317
00:34:06,628 --> 00:34:08,046
I offer you my condolences.

318
00:34:12,426 --> 00:34:13,552
Thank you.

319
00:34:22,102 --> 00:34:22,936
Wait.

320
00:34:24,688 --> 00:34:27,274
I didn't get to thank you properly.
Can I at least get your name?

321
00:34:27,357 --> 00:34:30,277
Or leave me the address
of your workplace--

322
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:31,361
Don't worry about it.

323
00:34:31,987 --> 00:34:33,906
I'm leaving for New York tomorrow anyway.

324
00:34:34,615 --> 00:34:35,449
What?

325
00:34:35,532 --> 00:34:37,367
You take care now, okay?

326
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:51,215
Great work, everyone.

327
00:34:52,424 --> 00:34:56,428
We had a few demanding VIP tables today,
so it would've been extra pressure.

328
00:34:57,054 --> 00:34:59,848
Still, we wrapped things up
without any serious mishaps.

329
00:35:00,432 --> 00:35:01,892
Well done, everyone.

330
00:35:03,602 --> 00:35:05,521
Especially Michael.

331
00:35:05,604 --> 00:35:06,814
Yes, Chef.

332
00:35:06,897 --> 00:35:09,024
We got a lot of compliments
on the main dish tonight.

333
00:35:09,858 --> 00:35:12,402
It must've been tough
to get the sweetbread just right.

334
00:35:12,903 --> 00:35:14,196
Nice work.

335
00:35:14,905 --> 00:35:15,781
Thank you, Chef.

336
00:35:16,448 --> 00:35:19,868
-Check the ingredients one last time…
-They use great ingredients, that's why.

337
00:35:19,952 --> 00:35:22,287
Double-check on everything,
then wrap up for tonight.

338
00:35:22,871 --> 00:35:24,081
-Thank you, Chef.
-Thank you, Chef.

339
00:35:27,084 --> 00:35:29,461
You all did well today.

340
00:35:30,379 --> 00:35:32,923
I could do with some grease
to wash down my smoky palate.

341
00:35:33,006 --> 00:35:34,258
How about some pork belly and soju?

342
00:35:37,010 --> 00:35:38,720
Don't drink too much though.

343
00:35:38,804 --> 00:35:40,681
We have another full house tomorrow, okay?

344
00:35:40,764 --> 00:35:41,640
-Okay!
-Okay!

345
00:35:41,723 --> 00:35:42,599
Clean up!

346
00:35:42,683 --> 00:35:45,519
-Let's clean up.
-Let's do this.

347
00:36:34,067 --> 00:36:35,444
Hey.

348
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:37,863
I'd heard, but seeing it for myself…

349
00:36:38,447 --> 00:36:40,365
Wow, your restaurant's pretty flashy.

350
00:36:43,660 --> 00:36:45,203
You look good, Woo-jin.

351
00:36:47,164 --> 00:36:50,083
Business must be good. You're glowing.

352
00:36:50,167 --> 00:36:51,335
How much?

353
00:36:51,418 --> 00:36:52,586
What?

354
00:36:52,669 --> 00:36:54,004
How much more

355
00:36:55,339 --> 00:36:56,298
do you need this time…

356
00:36:58,383 --> 00:36:59,801
that you came all the way here?

357
00:37:01,887 --> 00:37:02,846
Come on now.

358
00:37:04,389 --> 00:37:05,974
You're as impatient as ever.

359
00:37:06,808 --> 00:37:07,684
Listen.

360
00:37:09,102 --> 00:37:11,897
There's a proper order to things,
and a proper flow to a conversation.

361
00:37:11,980 --> 00:37:13,690
How many tables do you think I serve?

362
00:37:14,316 --> 00:37:17,152
I don't know… 12 or 13?

363
00:37:17,903 --> 00:37:19,112
There are exactly 15 tables.

364
00:37:20,906 --> 00:37:21,990
Each table

365
00:37:22,866 --> 00:37:25,202
seats two to four guests.

366
00:37:27,079 --> 00:37:29,915
For dinner alone,
the first round starts at 6 p.m.

367
00:37:30,540 --> 00:37:32,709
and the second round starts at 8 p.m.

368
00:37:33,502 --> 00:37:34,962
Tonight, we were fully booked.

369
00:37:35,045 --> 00:37:38,090
Even at only 4 guests for each table,
that's 60 per round.

370
00:37:38,173 --> 00:37:39,841
That's a total of 120.

371
00:37:39,925 --> 00:37:42,386
There are 20 servers covering the hall
and 15 cooks in the kitchen.

372
00:37:43,095 --> 00:37:46,473
We provide the best food and service
to almost ten times as many guests.

373
00:37:46,556 --> 00:37:48,558
We barely have time to sit down to rest,

374
00:37:48,642 --> 00:37:50,060
whether we burn our arms,

375
00:37:51,436 --> 00:37:54,648
cut our fingers on sharp knives,
sprain an ankle,

376
00:37:55,941 --> 00:37:57,442
or even end up in a cast.

377
00:37:57,526 --> 00:37:58,360
Why?

378
00:37:58,986 --> 00:38:00,570
Because once a customer
leaves disappointed…

379
00:38:02,656 --> 00:38:03,865
they never return.

380
00:38:08,578 --> 00:38:09,496
My point is…

381
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:15,961
it might look like
we dish everything up quickly and easily.

382
00:38:16,044 --> 00:38:19,339
But every second I spend arguing with you

383
00:38:20,716 --> 00:38:23,552
is time I should be spending
preparing for the best service tomorrow.

384
00:38:23,635 --> 00:38:26,138
You think I have time to waste
on a small-town bully like you?

385
00:38:29,141 --> 00:38:30,100
I don't.

386
00:38:32,060 --> 00:38:34,354
So quit wasting my time
and get to the point.

387
00:38:35,397 --> 00:38:36,314
That woman…

388
00:38:38,859 --> 00:38:40,736
How much did she tell you
to ask for this time?

389
00:38:52,706 --> 00:38:54,166
Don't worry too much.

390
00:38:54,791 --> 00:38:56,793
She'll only need to be hospitalized
for about ten days.

391
00:38:57,794 --> 00:38:59,629
Women your mom's age

392
00:38:59,713 --> 00:39:01,506
often suffer from hip joint injuries.

393
00:39:01,590 --> 00:39:05,385
Isn't it a relief
that she doesn't need surgery?

394
00:39:06,428 --> 00:39:08,930
Anyway, thanks again.

395
00:39:10,098 --> 00:39:12,100
You've taken a load off my mind.

396
00:39:12,184 --> 00:39:14,311
Oh, and I'll tell your mom

397
00:39:15,062 --> 00:39:16,813
to give you a call once she's discharged.

398
00:39:17,856 --> 00:39:19,816
You didn't say the name of the hospital.

399
00:39:23,820 --> 00:39:24,654
What?

400
00:39:27,574 --> 00:39:29,034
Are you afraid I'll visit?

401
00:39:35,499 --> 00:39:36,875
You punk.

402
00:39:37,709 --> 00:39:38,627
You're just the same.

403
00:39:41,713 --> 00:39:43,882
I guess a kid who killed his dad
really is something else.

404
00:39:51,014 --> 00:39:51,890
Man…

405
00:39:52,766 --> 00:39:54,392
You're shooting lasers out of your eyes.

406
00:39:55,977 --> 00:39:59,523
Who'd dare to talk to you
when you're looking like that?

407
00:40:07,489 --> 00:40:08,406
Thanks a lot.

408
00:40:24,422 --> 00:40:26,258
CHAIRWOMAN MOON

409
00:40:33,348 --> 00:40:34,182
Hello, ma'am.

410
00:40:34,266 --> 00:40:36,184
Are you still at the restaurant?

411
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:39,646
Yes. I'm almost done for the night.

412
00:40:41,314 --> 00:40:43,900
I see. You work late into the night.

413
00:40:46,027 --> 00:40:49,322
I heard Ms. Seon
meant to bring Mr. Bernier but couldn't.

414
00:40:50,073 --> 00:40:53,285
Yes. It looks like there was an issue.

415
00:40:54,077 --> 00:40:56,997
I reserved a table with you
because he was an important guest.

416
00:40:59,207 --> 00:41:02,377
Ms. Seon has been
working very hard for the company.

417
00:41:03,503 --> 00:41:05,046
No one's saying it,

418
00:41:06,173 --> 00:41:08,175
but everyone's on high alert.

419
00:41:09,759 --> 00:41:10,677
Right.

420
00:41:11,469 --> 00:41:13,847
Can you save us a table tomorrow evening?

421
00:41:13,930 --> 00:41:17,434
I'll escort Mr. Bernier myself.
Forget it if it's too big an ask.

422
00:41:18,643 --> 00:41:20,020
It's fine.

423
00:41:20,103 --> 00:41:21,605
I'll save you a table.

424
00:41:23,982 --> 00:41:25,734
Why do you sound so down?

425
00:41:26,401 --> 00:41:28,069
Are you unwell or something?

426
00:41:29,321 --> 00:41:30,322
No.

427
00:41:31,823 --> 00:41:33,533
I had a lot of customers today.

428
00:41:33,617 --> 00:41:35,744
I'm tired, that's all.

429
00:41:39,581 --> 00:41:43,001
I'll send you a month's worth
of herbal tonic this weekend.

430
00:41:43,084 --> 00:41:45,712
I'll tell Hwang to leave it
at your apartment's management office.

431
00:41:47,422 --> 00:41:49,716
I still have some left
from the last batch you sent.

432
00:41:49,799 --> 00:41:51,092
You shouldn't have any left.

433
00:41:51,176 --> 00:41:53,428
I told you to drink them regularly.

434
00:41:54,888 --> 00:41:56,139
Sorry.

435
00:41:56,806 --> 00:41:58,350
Be sure to drink one every day.

436
00:41:59,267 --> 00:42:02,103
You need to take better care of yourself
when you live alone.

437
00:42:02,187 --> 00:42:03,480
Right.

438
00:42:03,563 --> 00:42:05,357
I'm sorry to cause you concern.

439
00:42:05,440 --> 00:42:06,858
I'll see you tomorrow then.

440
00:42:07,609 --> 00:42:08,526
Bye.

441
00:42:09,110 --> 00:42:10,278
Yes, ma'am.

442
00:42:10,362 --> 00:42:11,363
Good night.

443
00:42:34,177 --> 00:42:35,095
You're home.

444
00:42:38,181 --> 00:42:39,599
Why are you back so late?

445
00:42:43,353 --> 00:42:44,646
Why am I back so late?

446
00:42:47,399 --> 00:42:48,984
I worked late, okay?

447
00:42:50,819 --> 00:42:54,114
Your husband's doing all he can
late into the night

448
00:42:54,197 --> 00:42:55,865
to earn a few more cents while you…

449
00:42:57,117 --> 00:42:58,368
You were fast asleep?

450
00:42:59,953 --> 00:43:00,912
What is it this time?

451
00:43:03,832 --> 00:43:05,125
Did you have a drink?

452
00:43:06,543 --> 00:43:07,669
With what money?

453
00:43:08,962 --> 00:43:12,382
Whether I drink with money I earned
or money I begged for,

454
00:43:12,966 --> 00:43:14,759
what does it concern you?

455
00:43:16,344 --> 00:43:17,345
Don't tell me

456
00:43:18,096 --> 00:43:19,347
you went to see him again?

457
00:43:22,142 --> 00:43:23,143
Did you?

458
00:43:24,227 --> 00:43:25,854
Did you go to his workplace again?

459
00:43:27,230 --> 00:43:28,690
What's gotten into you?

460
00:43:28,773 --> 00:43:30,859
Did you ask him for more money?

461
00:43:30,942 --> 00:43:34,738
Were you drinking and gambling all night
with the money you took from him?

462
00:43:34,821 --> 00:43:35,864
Damn it!

463
00:43:36,531 --> 00:43:38,158
How dare you question me?

464
00:43:38,241 --> 00:43:40,618
You're no cop or detective.

465
00:43:41,828 --> 00:43:44,205
You said you wouldn't bother him again.

466
00:43:45,749 --> 00:43:47,542
You said that would be the last time.

467
00:43:48,543 --> 00:43:49,586
Didn't you?

468
00:43:50,253 --> 00:43:52,422
Why do you keep bothering him?

469
00:43:52,505 --> 00:43:54,674
-You promised to leave him alone!
-Why you…

470
00:43:54,758 --> 00:43:57,385
Why bother him
when he's finally doing well?

471
00:43:57,469 --> 00:43:59,471
Why?

472
00:43:59,554 --> 00:44:01,056
How dare you… Let go of me!

473
00:44:01,139 --> 00:44:02,640
Do you still think you're a cop?

474
00:44:04,100 --> 00:44:06,311
You got fired for extortion.

475
00:44:07,062 --> 00:44:08,521
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

476
00:44:09,731 --> 00:44:11,441
Who the hell do you think you are?

477
00:44:11,524 --> 00:44:12,942
Do you have a death wish?

478
00:44:13,026 --> 00:44:13,985
Come here.

479
00:44:17,989 --> 00:44:18,990
Know your place.

480
00:44:19,866 --> 00:44:20,992
Don't talk back at me.

481
00:44:24,204 --> 00:44:26,706
I'm sorry. Please, I won't do it again.

482
00:44:28,208 --> 00:44:29,250
-Please!
-Damn it!

483
00:45:41,281 --> 00:45:42,115
Chef.

484
00:45:42,699 --> 00:45:43,616
You're still here?

485
00:45:44,325 --> 00:45:45,160
Yes, Chef.

486
00:45:45,910 --> 00:45:46,744
What about the team dinner?

487
00:45:48,872 --> 00:45:50,999
I had some things to sort out.

488
00:45:54,961 --> 00:45:56,004
What are you making?

489
00:45:56,087 --> 00:45:57,338
A beurre blanc, Chef.

490
00:45:57,964 --> 00:46:00,216
I tried adding a Korean citrus flavor.

491
00:46:00,300 --> 00:46:01,426
Like what?

492
00:46:01,509 --> 00:46:02,594
Persimmon vinegar.

493
00:46:03,887 --> 00:46:05,346
And toward the end,

494
00:46:05,430 --> 00:46:08,600
I added angelica leaves
instead of the usual herbs.

495
00:46:14,022 --> 00:46:16,691
It goes pretty well
with Korean freshwater fish.

496
00:46:16,774 --> 00:46:18,651
That's why I tried it.

497
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:35,001
Bae Yeong-su.

498
00:46:35,084 --> 00:46:35,960
Yes, Chef.

499
00:46:37,837 --> 00:46:38,838
How long has it been…

500
00:46:41,090 --> 00:46:42,300
since you joined Exception?

501
00:46:45,220 --> 00:46:47,347
Two more months,
and it'll be exactly three years.

502
00:46:49,807 --> 00:46:51,809
Head the fish station starting next month.

503
00:46:52,352 --> 00:46:53,186
Pardon?

504
00:46:54,604 --> 00:46:56,231
You've worked here long enough.

505
00:46:58,942 --> 00:47:01,110
Well, yes. Okay, Chef.

506
00:47:03,196 --> 00:47:04,531
Keep it to yourself for now.

507
00:47:05,198 --> 00:47:06,324
Understood, Chef.

508
00:47:09,327 --> 00:47:10,703
I'll do my best, Chef.

509
00:47:10,787 --> 00:47:11,746
Thank you.

510
00:47:20,004 --> 00:47:23,591
He never works as the head chef,
only as the sous-chef?

511
00:47:24,801 --> 00:47:26,302
Is that unusual or just plain weird?

512
00:47:26,886 --> 00:47:28,054
It's both.

513
00:47:28,721 --> 00:47:31,599
But he's too global to be called unusual

514
00:47:32,141 --> 00:47:34,227
and too cool to call weird.

515
00:47:34,310 --> 00:47:36,145
"Breaking down the border."

516
00:47:36,229 --> 00:47:38,898
"A chef of our time
that transcends borders,

517
00:47:38,982 --> 00:47:40,108
Chris K."

518
00:47:41,484 --> 00:47:42,527
It's a great headline.

519
00:47:43,027 --> 00:47:46,155
He hates the spotlight,
so there are very few photos of him.

520
00:47:47,282 --> 00:47:50,326
To think that you got to
try his food in Korea.

521
00:47:50,410 --> 00:47:51,411
I'm so jealous.

522
00:47:52,078 --> 00:47:53,162
Even here in New York,

523
00:47:53,246 --> 00:47:56,666
his restaurant is impossible to book
less than six months in advance.

524
00:47:57,500 --> 00:48:01,087
It's practically impossible now
since he left the US two years ago.

525
00:48:01,170 --> 00:48:02,422
So how was the food?

526
00:48:03,881 --> 00:48:05,758
It's really hard to describe.

527
00:48:06,593 --> 00:48:09,387
His cooking style
is definitely overpowering,

528
00:48:09,470 --> 00:48:11,431
but it also feels familiar.

529
00:48:12,015 --> 00:48:14,225
It's a bit like something
your mom would cook.

530
00:48:15,059 --> 00:48:18,313
I can't say.
I've never tasted anything like it before.

531
00:48:24,444 --> 00:48:25,278
Hold on.

532
00:48:31,117 --> 00:48:33,828
Cha Woo-jin came second?

533
00:48:35,580 --> 00:48:37,248
A few years ago, was it?

534
00:48:37,915 --> 00:48:42,670
The team representing his restaurant
won a culinary competition in Belgium.

535
00:48:42,754 --> 00:48:44,839
There was a huge gap
between first and second place

536
00:48:44,922 --> 00:48:46,257
that got everyone talking.

537
00:48:47,133 --> 00:48:49,677
What's funny is, the recipe they won with

538
00:48:49,761 --> 00:48:52,847
belonged to sous-chef Chris K.
and not the head chef.

539
00:48:53,348 --> 00:48:55,933
All the reporters ignored the head chef

540
00:48:56,017 --> 00:48:58,561
and flocked to Chris K. to talk to him.

541
00:49:02,523 --> 00:49:04,609
SEON JEONG-WON
CHIEF PRODUCER, TEAM 1

542
00:49:16,996 --> 00:49:17,914
You're looking for

543
00:49:19,040 --> 00:49:20,792
the best Korean chef?

544
00:49:25,922 --> 00:49:28,549
What does Pyeongyeon Group want with us?

545
00:49:40,228 --> 00:49:41,187
It's obvious.

546
00:49:42,772 --> 00:49:45,149
We want Famiglia to join the competition.

547
00:49:46,442 --> 00:49:47,276
I know

548
00:49:47,860 --> 00:49:50,071
how you feel about Pyeongyeon Group.

549
00:49:51,656 --> 00:49:53,991
No words could ever console you…

550
00:49:57,870 --> 00:50:00,039
and no excuses could clear up
the misunderstanding.

551
00:50:01,624 --> 00:50:02,458
Misunderstanding?

552
00:50:03,126 --> 00:50:04,669
Did you just call it a misunderstanding?

553
00:50:13,136 --> 00:50:14,804
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

554
00:50:19,225 --> 00:50:20,059
I know…

555
00:50:22,228 --> 00:50:24,188
why you people are
hosting this competition.

556
00:50:26,023 --> 00:50:28,151
It's not about
getting rid of Plate In Asia.

557
00:50:29,610 --> 00:50:33,114
It's to erase us, Famiglia and my dad.

558
00:50:35,867 --> 00:50:37,410
And your wrongdoings.

559
00:50:44,417 --> 00:50:47,920
Once the competition is over,
people will forget about Famiglia.

560
00:50:49,380 --> 00:50:51,966
And Choi Seung-hyo too,
who died fighting Pyeongyeon Group.

561
00:50:53,551 --> 00:50:54,385
Right?

562
00:50:56,179 --> 00:50:59,557
Whoever wins the competition
will hog the spotlight.

563
00:51:00,099 --> 00:51:03,060
Their restaurant will be fully booked
even before it opens

564
00:51:03,144 --> 00:51:06,147
and their life story will be on TV
while they film commercials.

565
00:51:08,107 --> 00:51:11,319
You'll use them
for all sorts of business opportunities.

566
00:51:13,404 --> 00:51:15,782
With that new puppet, Pyeongyeon Group…

567
00:51:17,784 --> 00:51:20,411
will gain everyone's attention,
and as always,

568
00:51:22,163 --> 00:51:23,998
you'll remain at the top.

569
00:51:31,839 --> 00:51:32,757
Ms. Choi.

570
00:51:43,893 --> 00:51:46,145
I've been planning this show
for five years,

571
00:51:46,979 --> 00:51:50,274
believing that Korean food can stand
at the heart of world cuisine.

572
00:51:51,692 --> 00:51:54,028
The corporate agenda you think I have?

573
00:51:56,239 --> 00:51:58,616
I have zero intention
of sacrificing my show

574
00:51:59,992 --> 00:52:01,035
for some corporate agenda.

575
00:52:02,578 --> 00:52:03,412
So please.

576
00:52:03,496 --> 00:52:04,956
Reconsider my proposition.

577
00:52:05,623 --> 00:52:08,501
I want Famiglia to enter the competition.

578
00:52:11,921 --> 00:52:14,048
Sure. I understand.

579
00:52:15,216 --> 00:52:16,926
I appreciate the offer…

580
00:52:18,761 --> 00:52:21,013
but do you think we could enter?

581
00:52:24,684 --> 00:52:25,852
Look around.

582
00:52:27,937 --> 00:52:29,397
We don't even have a head chef.

583
00:52:33,067 --> 00:52:34,026
That man from yesterday.

584
00:52:35,069 --> 00:52:35,903
What?

585
00:52:36,529 --> 00:52:39,490
The man who cooked
the incredible food yesterday.

586
00:52:41,200 --> 00:52:42,660
He's the hottest Korean chef

587
00:52:43,494 --> 00:52:45,246
in the whole world right now.

588
00:52:47,373 --> 00:52:48,416
Chris K.

589
00:52:53,713 --> 00:52:55,631
What is it that you really want?

590
00:52:56,966 --> 00:52:59,218
To win a lawsuit against Pyeongyeon Group?

591
00:53:01,470 --> 00:53:05,182
Isn't your father
and Famiglia's name and honor

592
00:53:05,266 --> 00:53:07,560
much more important than that?

593
00:53:12,064 --> 00:53:14,233
No one knows
how long the lawsuit will take,

594
00:53:14,317 --> 00:53:16,944
and going up against Pyeongyeon
will cost you a fortune.

595
00:53:17,028 --> 00:53:18,863
The longer it drags on,

596
00:53:18,946 --> 00:53:20,990
the more people will forget.

597
00:53:21,490 --> 00:53:24,243
Not just Chef Choi Seung-hyo,
but also Famiglia.

598
00:53:29,165 --> 00:53:30,541
Win the competition.

599
00:53:31,292 --> 00:53:34,503
Then you'll restore
your father and Famiglia's honor,

600
00:53:35,421 --> 00:53:37,673
and people will listen
to what you have to say.

601
00:53:38,424 --> 00:53:41,344
Winning the competition
is how you keep Famiglia alive.

602
00:53:41,427 --> 00:53:42,261
Listen to me.

603
00:53:43,512 --> 00:53:44,764
Get Chris K.

604
00:53:46,349 --> 00:53:50,019
Then you can save Famiglia
and restore your father's honor.

605
00:53:52,521 --> 00:53:54,148
It won't be too late
to sue Pyeongyeon then.

606
00:53:56,776 --> 00:53:57,610
Look.

607
00:53:59,695 --> 00:54:02,239
I'm offering you a deal, Ms. Choi.

608
00:54:04,700 --> 00:54:06,827
A deal that stakes both Pyeongyeon Group…

609
00:54:10,373 --> 00:54:11,207
and Famiglia.

610
00:54:22,009 --> 00:54:23,511
TIME PULLS US APART

611
00:54:57,378 --> 00:54:58,254
Wait!

612
00:55:05,594 --> 00:55:06,429
Yesterday at Famiglia.

613
00:55:10,391 --> 00:55:11,308
What are you doing here?

614
00:55:13,602 --> 00:55:17,648
I was so distracted yesterday
that I didn't get to thank you properly.

615
00:55:19,316 --> 00:55:20,359
What?

616
00:55:21,193 --> 00:55:23,863
I remembered you saying
you were leaving for New York today,

617
00:55:23,946 --> 00:55:24,947
so I came here.

618
00:55:30,077 --> 00:55:31,328
Help me.

619
00:55:38,919 --> 00:55:40,588
The best K-chef?

620
00:55:42,173 --> 00:55:44,216
I get what you're after, but I can't help.

621
00:55:46,844 --> 00:55:48,804
I'm starting a new job
the day after tomorrow.

622
00:55:50,806 --> 00:55:52,725
If I don't leave today,

623
00:55:52,808 --> 00:55:55,394
I'll have to pay a huge penalty
for breach of contract.

624
00:56:06,489 --> 00:56:08,115
Even if I entered,

625
00:56:09,116 --> 00:56:10,743
there's no guarantee we'd win.

626
00:56:11,327 --> 00:56:13,537
Besides, I'm not the person
to represent Famiglia.

627
00:56:14,830 --> 00:56:17,708
There's no time to prepare,
and you have no staff.

628
00:56:19,585 --> 00:56:22,421
Anyway, it's just not possible.

629
00:56:24,799 --> 00:56:26,509
Let's go. I have to board soon.

630
00:56:37,770 --> 00:56:39,438
Pyeongyeon killed my father.

631
00:56:41,982 --> 00:56:43,859
Pyeongyeon Group killed him.

632
00:56:43,943 --> 00:56:47,363
They fabricated everything
and drove him to take his own life.

633
00:56:52,910 --> 00:56:54,161
I know exactly why

634
00:56:54,912 --> 00:56:57,498
they want to host this competition.

635
00:56:58,374 --> 00:57:00,918
They're trying to cover up my dad's death.

636
00:57:01,544 --> 00:57:04,380
They'll make sure
whoever represents them wins.

637
00:57:04,463 --> 00:57:06,215
That's what Pyeongyeon always does.

638
00:57:06,715 --> 00:57:09,343
They eliminate whoever
and whatever gets in their way,

639
00:57:09,426 --> 00:57:12,346
and they fill their ranks
with people who take their side.

640
00:57:14,348 --> 00:57:15,224
Help me.

641
00:57:17,643 --> 00:57:21,105
I want to show them for once,
even if it's just once,

642
00:57:21,939 --> 00:57:24,066
that they can't always have their way.

643
00:57:26,277 --> 00:57:28,654
I want to prove it to my late father.

644
00:57:29,780 --> 00:57:32,533
I want to prove it to those
who killed my father.

645
00:57:35,161 --> 00:57:36,704
Pyeongyeon killed my father.

646
00:57:36,787 --> 00:57:38,414
Pyeongyeon killed Dad.

647
00:57:47,840 --> 00:57:49,133
Pyeongyeon killed Dad.

648
00:57:49,216 --> 00:57:51,886
Pyeongyeon killed Dad!

649
00:58:32,009 --> 00:58:33,594
Let me out!

650
00:58:47,441 --> 00:58:49,068
Dad!

651
00:58:50,277 --> 00:58:51,445
Dad!

652
00:58:51,528 --> 00:58:52,947
Open your eyes, Han!

653
00:58:53,030 --> 00:58:55,532
Wake up, Han. Kang Han!

654
00:59:14,510 --> 00:59:16,512
You'll die too if you stay here.

655
00:59:17,221 --> 00:59:18,305
Do as I say.

656
00:59:18,389 --> 00:59:20,099
Listen to me now.

657
00:59:21,141 --> 00:59:22,434
Go!

658
00:59:27,856 --> 00:59:29,358
Pyeongyeon killed my dad.

659
00:59:29,441 --> 00:59:30,818
Pyeongyeon killed Dad.

660
00:59:32,111 --> 00:59:33,821
Pyeongyeon killed Dad!

661
00:59:35,030 --> 00:59:36,782
Pyeongyeon killed him!

662
00:59:39,326 --> 00:59:40,160
No.

663
00:59:41,870 --> 00:59:42,955
Not now.

664
00:59:46,333 --> 00:59:47,376
Are you okay?

665
00:59:52,798 --> 00:59:53,757
Are you all right?

666
00:59:58,721 --> 00:59:59,555
Can you get up?

667
01:00:25,914 --> 01:00:26,999
Are you okay?

668
01:00:30,711 --> 01:00:31,920
Do you know who I am?

669
01:00:45,684 --> 01:00:48,020
The reason Pyeongyeon Group

670
01:00:48,604 --> 01:00:51,357
decided to scrap
the long-standing Plate In Asia system

671
01:00:51,440 --> 01:00:53,734
boils down to just one phrase.

672
01:00:54,401 --> 01:00:55,819
"Our original mindset."

673
01:00:57,071 --> 01:01:01,116
Before that, there is no room
for authority, tradition, or history.

674
01:01:04,370 --> 01:01:06,330
As of this moment,

675
01:01:06,413 --> 01:01:08,832
we're going back to where we first began,

676
01:01:09,500 --> 01:01:10,918
to when we searched for

677
01:01:11,001 --> 01:01:13,629
the best Korean cuisine
and the best Korean chefs.

678
01:01:14,546 --> 01:01:17,049
We're leaving the grading system behind
to focus on people.

679
01:01:17,132 --> 01:01:18,550
We're casting off the shell

680
01:01:18,634 --> 01:01:21,136
to return to the essence of cooking.

681
01:01:25,265 --> 01:01:28,394
This competition
is not for Pyeongyeon Group.

682
01:01:28,477 --> 01:01:32,940
It is for our future
and the future of K-food in the world.

683
01:01:34,358 --> 01:01:37,152
The future of Korean cuisine
is in your hands.

684
01:01:37,236 --> 01:01:41,323
Join us
at The Table: K-Chef 2026.

685
01:01:54,128 --> 01:01:54,962
Han!

686
01:01:55,045 --> 01:01:57,131
-Over there!
-There he is!

687
01:01:57,214 --> 01:01:58,841
Hurry! Get him!

688
01:01:59,675 --> 01:02:00,509
Stop!

689
01:02:02,511 --> 01:02:04,388
Hurry! Catch him!

690
01:02:06,348 --> 01:02:08,142
-Hey! Where is he going?
-Get him!

691
01:02:15,524 --> 01:02:16,775
Wait!

692
01:03:12,289 --> 01:03:13,165
Wait.

693
01:03:14,541 --> 01:03:15,959
Hey, hold on.

694
01:03:17,377 --> 01:03:18,795
The boarding gates are that way.

695
01:03:35,646 --> 01:03:36,480
Let's do it.

696
01:03:37,814 --> 01:03:39,900
What? Do what?

697
01:03:39,983 --> 01:03:41,026
Let's do it together.

698
01:03:42,319 --> 01:03:44,696
The Table: K-Chef 2026.

699
01:04:31,493 --> 01:04:32,911
Cooking is about teamwork.

700
01:04:32,995 --> 01:04:34,621
That's not the right sizzle.

701
01:04:34,705 --> 01:04:37,082
I've never cooked before,
and I'm useless at it.

702
01:04:37,165 --> 01:04:39,626
The requirement is a team of four.

703
01:04:39,710 --> 01:04:40,669
RESUME

704
01:04:40,752 --> 01:04:42,838
Even if we start practicing
around the clock now,

705
01:04:42,921 --> 01:04:44,464
there's no guarantee
we'll pass the preliminary round.

706
01:04:44,548 --> 01:04:45,882
The star of that show

707
01:04:46,466 --> 01:04:49,136
should be someone we cast.

708
01:04:49,219 --> 01:04:51,054
I was expecting a few stragglers.

709
01:04:51,680 --> 01:04:52,681
This should be interesting.

710
01:04:53,807 --> 01:04:54,641
Roll the cameras.

711
01:04:54,725 --> 01:04:57,311
Let the competition begin!

712
01:04:57,394 --> 01:04:59,062
Because in the end,

713
01:04:59,771 --> 01:05:00,981
you'll lose to me again anyway.

714
01:05:07,404 --> 01:05:10,407
Subtitle: Jennifer Jean Lim
